From 52acd47448b46644fc9807f5ab04d40b84f4f6cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:40:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-nubia-nx809j: don't hand the
 Wi-Fi link to the ADSP

On Kaanapali the vendor kernel hands the PCIe link to CESTA (pcie_crm,
the PCIe state machine and PDC), not to the ADSP. The ADSP acks the
pcie_drv hand-off but doesn't hold the link: with wake-on-WLAN armed
the phone reset into EDL about 20 s into sleep, once the Wi-Fi chip
woke the link with the host's clocks and votes gone.

Drop qcom,drv-supported until CESTA is supported. WAKE# stays on the
controller.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts
index d7ac83dc22b4..81aba9a7db90 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts
@@ -1813,11 +1813,14 @@ &mdss_dsi0_phy {
 
 &pcie0 {
 	/*
-	 * The ADSP holds the Wi-Fi link through suspend. WAKE# belongs to the
-	 * controller, which arms it only while the Wi-Fi chip is armed for
-	 * wake: an unarmed chip is powered off in suspend and drags it low.
+	 * WAKE# belongs to the controller, which arms it only while the Wi-Fi
+	 * chip is armed for wake: an unarmed chip is powered off in suspend
+	 * and drags it low.
+	 *
+	 * No qcom,drv-supported: on Kaanapali the link is handed over to CESTA
+	 * (pcie_crm), not the ADSP. The ADSP acks the hand-off but doesn't
+	 * hold the link, and the phone resets once the Wi-Fi chip wakes it.
 	 */
-	qcom,drv-supported;
 	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pcie0_default_state>;
-- 
2.56.0

